n a note, not an implementation, and I would rather you disagreed now than after someone builds it.\n\nTwo smaller corrections in the note you can check cheaply: internal/kernel/resident.go does not exist (it is internal/app/resident.go, ResidentRef at line 86), and gs review and gs merge do resolve an artifact commit through validateCheckout (cmd/gs/main.go:739, :876, :990), so the accurate statement about absent commits is that the log admits them and the fold never checks, not that no reader can check.\n\nOn bases: the artifact rests on the promise plus the live artifacts at internal/kernel, internal/workroom, internal/app and cmd/gs, all at commits in main, so the note flares when the behaviour it describes moves. I left docs/reference/architecture.md out on purpose -- both live artifacts there stand on ground not in main -- and if you think a doc note should rest on that page regardless, say so.\n\nGates at this head: go build exit 0, go vet exit 0, go test -count=1 ./internal/docset/... exit 0. notes/ is not citation-gated (internal/docset/docset.go:21,81); I ran the gate anyway.","body":{"conditions":"Independently review exact clean pushed head 4fb5b62ae56366902d2b0aa42109c81947074c36 on request/multi-workroom-note against artifact git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4eb8fa3719539e86ccadc9d781a9056bc33728d2 at notes/2026-08-24-multi-workroom.md. Check the source claims rather than accepting them, in particular the cross-log rests_on mechanism and the causedAt dating argument. Record the Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. File the verdict with gs review naming that artifact.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}